102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"6.W.7.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"6.W.8","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"6.W.8.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[1,"128.21(b)(1)(A)","listen actively to interpret a message, ask clarifying questions, and respond appropriately;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.21(b)(1)(B)","follow and give oral instructions that include multiple action steps;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.21(b)(1)(C)","give an organized presentation with a specific stance and position, employing eye contact, speaking rate, volume, enunciation, natural gestures, and conventions of language to communicate ideas effectively; and","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.21(b)(1)(D)","participate in student-led discussions by eliciting and considering suggestions from other group members, taking notes, and identifying points of agreement and disagreement.","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.21(b)(2)(A)","demonstrate and apply phonetic knowledge by: (i) differentiating between commonly confused terms such as porque/porqué/por qué/por que, asimismo (adverbio)/así mismo (de la misma manera), sino/si no, and también/tan bien; (ii) decoding palabras agudas, graves, esdrújulas, and sobresdrújulas (words with the stress on the last, penultimate, and antepenultimate syllable and words with the stress on the syllable before the antepenultimate); (iii) decoding words with hiatus and diphthongs; and (iv) using knowledge of syllable division patterns and morphemes to decode multisyllabic words;","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.21(b)(2)(B)","demonstrate and apply spelling knowledge by: (i) spelling palabras agudas, graves, esdrújulas, and sobresdrújulas (words with the stress on the antepenultimate, penultimate, and ultimate/last syllable and words with the stress on the syllable before the antepenultimate); (ii) marking accents appropriately when conjugating verbs in simple and imperfect past, perfect conditional, and future tenses; and (iii) spelling words with diphthongs and hiatus; and","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.21(b)(2)(C)","write legibly in cursive.","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.21(b)(3)(A)","use print or digital resources to determine the meaning, syllabication, pronunciation, word origin, and part of speech;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.21(b)(3)(B)","use context such as definition, analogy, and examples to clarify the meaning of words;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.21(b)(3)(C)","determine the meaning and usage of grade-level academic Spanish words derived from Greek and Latin roots, including metro-, grafo-, scrib-, and port-; and","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.21(b)(3)(D)","differentiate between and use homographs, homophones, and commonly confused terms such as porque/porqué/por qué/por que, sino/si no, and también/tan bien.","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.21(b)(4)","Developing and sustaining foundational language skills: listening, speaking, reading, writing, and thinking--fluency. The student reads grade-level text with fluency and comprehension. The student is expected to adjust fluency when reading grade-level text based on the reading purpose.","strand","4",null],[1,"128.21(b)(5)","Developing and sustaining foundational language skills: listening, speaking, reading, writing, and thinking--self-sustained reading. The student reads grade-appropriate texts independently. The student is expected to self-select text and read independently for a sustained period of time.","strand","5",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(A)","establish purpose for reading assigned and self-selected text;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(B)","generate questions about text before, during, and after reading to deepen understanding and gain information;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(C)","make and correct or confirm predictions using text features, characteristics of genre, and structures;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(D)","create mental images to deepen understanding;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(E)","make connections to personal experiences, ideas in other texts, and society;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(F)","make inferences and use evidence to support understanding;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(G)","evaluate details read to determine key ideas;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(H)","synthesize information to create new understanding; and","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(6)(I)","monitor comprehension and make adjustments such as re-reading, using background knowledge, asking questions, and annotating when understanding breaks down.","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(A)","describe personal connections to a variety of sources, including self-selected texts;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(B)","write responses that demonstrate understanding of texts, including comparing sources within and across genres;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(C)","use text evidence to support an appropriate response;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(D)","paraphrase and summarize texts in ways that maintain meaning and logical order;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(E)","interact with sources in meaningful ways such as notetaking, annotating, freewriting, or illustrating;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(F)","respond using newly acquired vocabulary as appropriate;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(G)","discuss and write about the explicit or implicit meanings of text;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(H)","respond orally or in writing with appropriate register, vocabulary, tone, and voice; and","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(7)(I)","reflect on and adjust responses as new evidence is presented.","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.21(b)(8)(A)","infer multiple themes within and across texts using text evidence;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.21(b)(8)(B)","analyze how the characters' internal and external responses develop the plot;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.21(b)(8)(C)","analyze plot elements, including rising action, climax, falling action, resolution, and non- linear elements such as flashback; and","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.21(b)(8)(D)","analyze how the setting, including historical and cultural settings, influences character and plot development.","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.21(b)(9)(A)","demonstrate knowledge of literary genres such as realistic fiction, adventure stories, historical fiction, mysteries, humor, and myths;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.21(b)(9)(B)","analyze the effect of meter and structural elements such as line breaks in poems across a variety of poetic forms;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.21(b)(9)(C)","analyze how playwrights develop characters through dialogue and staging;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.21(b)(9)(D)","analyze characteristics and structural elements of informational text, including: (i) the controlling idea or thesis with supporting evidence; (ii) features such as introduction, foreword, preface, references, or acknowledgements to gain background information; and (iii) organizational patterns such as definition, classification, advantage, and disadvantage;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.21(b)(9)(E)","analyze characteristics and structures of argumentative text by: (i) identifying the claim; (ii) explaining how the author uses various types of evidence to support the argument; and (iii) identifying the intended audience or reader; and","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.21(b)(9)(F)","analyze characteristics of multimodal and digital texts.","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.21(b)(10)(A)","explain the author's purpose and message within a text;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.21(b)(10)(B)","analyze how the use of text structure contributes to the author's purpose;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.21(b)(10)(C)","analyze the author's use of print and graphic features to achieve specific purposes;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.21(b)(10)(D)","describe how the author's use of figurative language such as metaphor and personification achieves specific purposes;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.21(b)(10)(E)","identify the use of literary devices, including omniscient and limited point of view, to achieve a specific purpose;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.21(b)(10)(F)","analyze how the author's use of language contributes to mood and voice; and","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.21(b)(10)(G)","explain the differences between rhetorical devices and logical fallacies.","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.21(b)(11)(A)","plan a first draft by selecting a genre appropriate for a particular topic, purpose, and audience using a range of strategies such as discussion, background reading, and personal interests;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.21(b)(11)(B)","develop drafts into a focused, structured, and coherent piece of writing by: (i) organizing with purposeful structure, including an introduction, transitions, coherence within and across paragraphs, and a conclusion; and (ii) developing an engaging idea reflecting depth of thought with specific facts and details;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.21(b)(11)(C)","revise drafts for clarity, development, organization, style, word choice, and sentence variety;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.21(b)(11)(D)","edit drafts using standard Spanish conventions, including: (i) complete complex sentences with subject-verb agreement and avoidance of splices, run-ons, and fragments; (ii) consistent, appropriate use of verb tenses; (iii) conjunctive adverbs; (iv) prepositions and prepositional phrases and their influence on subject-verb agreement; (v) pronouns, including personal, possessive, objective, reflexive, prepositional, indefinite, and relative; (vi) subordinating conjunctions to form complex sentences and correlative conjunctions; (vii) capitalization of proper nouns, including abbreviations, initials, acronyms, and organizations; (viii) punctuation marks, including commas in complex sentences, transitions, and introductory elements; and (ix) correct spelling, including commonly confused terms; and","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.21(b)(11)(E)","publish written work for appropriate audiences.","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.21(b)(12)(A)","compose literary texts such as personal narratives, fiction, and poetry using genre characteristics and craft;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.21(b)(12)(B)","compose informational texts, including multi-paragraph essays that convey information about a topic, using a clear controlling idea or thesis statement and genre characteristics and craft;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.21(b)(12)(C)","compose multi-paragraph argumentative texts using genre characteristics and craft; and","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.21(b)(12)(D)","compose correspondence that reflects an opinion, registers a complaint, or requests information in a business or friendly structure.","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(A)","generate student-selected and teacher-guided questions for formal and informal inquiry;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(B)","develop and revise a plan;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(C)","refine the major research question, if necessary, guided by the answers to a secondary set of questions;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(D)","identify and gather relevant information from a variety of sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(E)","differentiate between primary and secondary sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(F)","synthesize information from a variety of sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(G)","differentiate between paraphrasing and plagiarism when using source materials;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(H)","examine sources for: (i) reliability, credibility, and bias; and (ii) faulty reasoning such as hyperbole, emotional appeals, and stereotype;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(I)","display academic citations and use source materials ethically; and","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.21(b)(13)(J)","use an appropriate mode of delivery, whether written, oral, or multimodal, to present results.","expectation","13",null]]}